A||||13||85ZainoGT||Reverse lights stopped working||||5||
Z||000000||85ZainoGT||09-20-2001||09:15 PM||||any ideas?||||reg||5
Z||000001||LS1swap||09-20-2001||09:22 PM||||is it a stick or auto I know on the stick for an 85 the switch that controls the back up lights is under the shift console, i know for it went bad on my 86 four speed and I had to replace it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||85ZainoGT||09-20-2001||09:26 PM||||yes its a stick, how do I take out the console and where and what do I need to buy, how much? thanks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||grgoyl86||09-20-2001||10:31 PM||||Hold on, before you take the console apart. Is this an Isuzu tranny? If so, the switch is on the tranny, not in the console.<P>------------------<BR><B>Bob Schlag</B><BR><I>Mid Atlantic Fiero Owners Association</I><BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieropride.com</A><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ani_interior.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||09-21-2001||12:07 AM||||85ZainoGT,<P>You have an 85, right?<BR>Remove the shifter console by removing the 4 7mm screws found under the ashtrays (they lift out). Unscrew the shifter knob and remove. Lift off shifter housing with plate. There you will see a small black box, this is your back up light switch. The plunger should close its contact switch when the shifter is in the reverse position. If it doesn't try to adjust it so that it does. If they still won't work, get a new switch.||||reg||1
Z||000005||sqoach||09-21-2001||11:23 AM||||Did both lights work, then now they don't? If so it's most likely the switch. I don't think both bulbs will burn out at the same time. Also, do you turn signals work? If not, check your fuse. And to check the switch, do what Indiana_resto_guy says.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif">          <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*SOLD(?)*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||SLYGUY||09-21-2001||11:48 PM||||Backup lights don't work on my 88GT.<P>It has the Getrag 5spd. The turn signals work, so it's not the fuse.<BR>Where is the switch?<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000007||sqoach||09-22-2001||05:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SLYGUY:<BR><B>Backup lights don't work on my 88GT.<P>It has the Getrag 5spd. The turn signals work, so it's not the fuse.<BR>Where is the switch?<P>Sly</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The switch is in the tranny. Kind of a pain to get to. You'll want to get an oxygen sensor socket if you don't have one. The reason is because the "switch" has a wire coming out of it, so you can't use a regular socket. You might be able to use a wrench, but that would be a pain in the a$$. I'll get a pic if you need one. I don't have the getrag, but I have a 5 spd that has the switch in the tranny. I think they're in the same place.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif">          <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*SOLD(?)*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000008||SLYGUY||09-22-2001||06:23 PM||||Thanks for the info Adam. <P>A picture would help me out. Can you post it?<P>Thanks!!<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000009||sqoach||09-22-2001||10:32 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SLYGUY:<BR><B>Thanks for the info Adam. <P>A picture would help me out. Can you post it?<P>Thanks!!<P>Sly</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sure. Not sure if I can get one on here tonight. If not, I'll get one tomorrow.||||reg||1
Z||000010||SLYGUY||09-23-2001||01:03 AM||||Thanks Adam,<P>I'll watch for it.<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000011||Shiner||09-23-2001||06:05 PM||||On the getrag, the switch is located right under the shift linkage bracket, on the trans case.  I got it out with a wrench pretty easily.  Just hop in the trunk and go to work!  ||||reg||1
